1
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,940
[ Kazoos ]

2
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:00,460
Hey, how's it going, Frank ?

3
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:04,520
Not so good. I can't seem to get
this photon channeler working.

4
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:06,530
Well, you'd better
figure it out.

5
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:10,360
- The colonel wants to show
the system to the top brass next month.
- I know, I know.

6
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:20,910
[ Men Shouting ]

7
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:22,910
-[ Loud Bang ]
- What was that ?

8
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,140
- What's that sound out there ?
- [ Alarm Blaring ]

9
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,810
It's a break-in !
Erase the access code !

10
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:30,250
X-Y-4--

11
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:48,070
[ Gasps ]

12
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,730
[ Both Groan ]

13
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:52,740
[ Alarm Continues
Blaring, Stops ]

14
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,740
All clear.

15
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:02,880
Neatly done, Fernlick.

16
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:05,550
- It's, uh, Fenwick, sir.
- Oh.

17
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:08,250
- Are they dead ?
- No, sir. Merely unconscious.

18
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:11,420
Good, good.
You know how I hate violence.

19
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,490
Mmm. Nice shine.

20
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,560
-Uh, what next, sir ?
-Well, obviously, we establish our base.

21
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:19,660
- And where will that be ?
- The last place on Earth they'd look.

22
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:23,670
A place called...
3rd Street School.

23
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,420
Last day of school sale,
boys and girls.

24
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:13,420
Get your celebratory
contraband right here.

25
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:16,930
Shaving cream, T.P., goofy string,
maps of the teachers' houses.

26
00:03:16,990 --> 00:03:19,930
I'll take one of them maps,
Hustler Kid.

27
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,060
Hey, Diggers, let's party.

28
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:25,070
Can't now. Gotta finish filling up
our holes before the end of the day.

29
00:03:25,130 --> 00:03:28,070
Won't be able to dig 'em up next year
if we don't fill 'em now.

30
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:31,400
[ Spitting ]
Hey ! Big kids bury me !

31
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:33,240
Oops.

32
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:37,750
I, King Bob, in my last official
act before entering middle school,

33
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:40,750
hereby anoint this boy here
King Freddie the Second.

34
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:43,750
May you boss around
all of the kids with fairness.

35
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,410
The king has graduated !
Long live the king !

36
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,120
- [ Cheering ]
-    [ "Hail to the Chief" ]

37
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:52,130
Elbow up !
Eyes forward !

38
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,130
You call that kazoo playing ?

39
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:57,290
- Ah, ceremony.
- I'm, like, moved, Ashley A.

40
00:03:57,370 --> 00:04:00,230
Say what you want about their
personal lives, Ashley Q.

41
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:02,900
The royals have such style.

42
00:04:02,970 --> 00:04:04,910
Keep 'em comin' !
Let's go !

43
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:08,970
Ms. Finster, the kids are practically
mad with last-day-of-school fever !

44
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:11,480
Of course they are, Randall.
They're animals living by pure instinct.

45
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:13,980
I've got a list
of infractions a mile long:

46
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:15,980
The Diggers
hit a water main,

47
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:18,320
- the kindergarteners
are feasting on paste,
- Never mind, Randall.

48
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:21,320
Hustler Kid is, uh--
Did you say "never mind" ?

49
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:24,330
That's right, Randall. What I've
got here is bigger, much bigger.

50
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:28,800
All this year I've been holding
back on the ice cream, hiding it
from all those little savages.

51
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:32,820
Just look at it, Randall.
I'm counting 1 00, maybe 200 cases of it.

52
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:35,100
What are you going to do
with all those ice creams ?

53
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:37,110
Sell 'em back to the district,
of course.

54
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:39,940
Think of all the chalk
and erasers we can get.

55
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:42,440
But, Ms. Finster,
I've got dirt on everybody.

56
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:45,450
Well, everybody except
Detweiler and his pals.

57
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,350
Come to think of it,
I haven't seen those guys anywhere.

58
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,350
Ah, forget about 'em, Randall.

59
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:54,360
There's nothing T.j. Detweiler and his
hooligan friends can do to stop me now.

60
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:04,030
Well, that should do it.
There's enough here for everyone.

61
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,630
Good. Then it's party time.

62
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,300
Kids of the playground !

63
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,470
I give you ice cream !

64
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:18,100
Pull !

65
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:20,950
[ Cheering ]

66
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:24,790
- Ice cream !
- Choco-pops !
- Fudge bars !

67
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:26,520
Fudgsicle !

68
00:05:26,590 --> 00:05:28,780
My ice cream !

69
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,790
Stop it !
Stop it, I say !

70
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:32,790
You little monsters
are in trouble now !

71
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:36,530
-just wait'll Principal Prickly
finds out about this !
-Attention, students!

72
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,300
- This is Principal Prickly talking.
- Ooh, that was fast.

73
00:05:39,370 --> 00:05:42,810
Some of you may have noticed
ice cream on the playground.

74
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:46,210
I will not stand for this. This
ice cream should be eaten immediately.

75
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,210
Huh ?

76
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,040
[ Cheering ]

77
00:05:50,110 --> 00:05:53,210
In addition, I want you all to ignore
Ms. Finster, no matter what she says...

78
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,220
about ice cream
or anything else.

79
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,550
- [ Cheering Continues ]
- [ Muttering ] This can't be happening.

80
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:01,490
Furthermore, I want to inform you
all that I have a fat, saggy butt...

81
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,490
which I like to scratch
every hour on the hour.

82
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,830
Also, I want to apologize
to all of you...

83
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:14,060
for being such a mean principal,
taking away hall passes,
giving guys recess detention,

84
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:18,300
refusing to accept sick notes
just 'cause it doesn't look
like a guy's mom's signature,

85
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:21,810
making kids stand at the wall
for ten whole minutes, with no break!

86
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:25,110
Man, I feel ashamed of myself for all
the terrible, rotten things I've done.

87
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,120
And next year,
I promise to--

88
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:34,120
Why, Principal Prickly, sir,
what a surprise.

89
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:40,160
Why do you do this to me, Detweiler ?
Do you enjoy tormenting me ?

90
00:06:40,230 --> 00:06:43,960
- Do you hate me ?
- On the contrary, sir, I have
the utmost respect for you.

91
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:47,700
Don't be smart with me, boy. All year
long you've been pushing me, testing me.

92
00:06:47,770 --> 00:06:50,470
- I don't know what you mean, sir.
- Oh, really ?

93
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:54,240
How about the time you convinced
the F.B.I. I was a Chinese agent
and got me arrested ?

94
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:58,370
You were giving us a speech on
personal hygiene. You had to be stopped.

95
00:06:58,450 --> 00:07:01,880
How about the time
you forged my signature
and ordered a motorboat for the school ?

96
00:07:01,950 --> 00:07:05,550
It was for the kindergarteners.
Owning a boat's always been
kind of a dream of theirs.

97
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:10,290
I've had enough of your pranks.
This time I'm really gonna
throw the book at you.

98
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:13,490
With all due respect, sir, you'd better
get throwing, 'cause you're out of time.

99
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:15,500
- Huh ?
- It's the last day of school, sir.

100
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:18,090
I've only got 20 more seconds
of fourth grade left. Look.

101
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,770
In some ways, people,
this day is a bummer for me.

102
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,170
But in other ways
it's the ultimate high,

103
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,610
because every milestone that you kids
pass is another step towards--

104
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,010
- Uh, Miss Grotke ?
- Yes, Spinelli ?

105
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,450
I don't mean
to interrupt, but--

106
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:39,680
Oh, yes !
Be my guest.

107
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:45,520
[ Kids In Unison ]
Six, five, four, three, two, one--

108
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,460
-[ Bell Rings ]
- [ Cheering ]

109
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:52,260
- Whoo !
- Whoo-hoo !

110
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:54,830
[ Laughing ]
Yeah !

111
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,840
[ Together]
Scandalous !

112
00:07:56,910 --> 00:08:01,670
Calling out around the world
Are you ready for a brand-new beat

113
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:04,540
-  Summer's here
- You eat paste ! You eat paste !

114
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:08,050
And the time is right
for dancin'in the street

115
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,050
-    [ Stops ]
- Hey ! No running in the halls !

116
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:13,710
Yeah, what's the big deal ?
It's just the end of the school year.

117
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:16,520
[ Together]
The end of the school year ?
- Whoo-hoo !

118
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:18,890
It doesn't matter
what you wear

119
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:22,060
- Whoo-hoo ! [ Laughing ]
-  Just as long as you are there

120
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:26,160
Girls, what shall we do with
the rest of this corn chowder ?

121
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:30,570
[ Sniffs ] Aw, leave it in the kettle.
It'll keep till September.

122
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:33,400
- [ All Laughing ]
-   They'll be dancing
Dancing in the street

123
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:37,410
-   They're dancin'in the street
-  Dancing in the street

124
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,570
See you next year,
Principal Prickly.

125
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:43,090
You'd better do some
growing up this summer, young man.

126
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:45,250
[ Sighs ]
I hate my job.

127
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:48,090
There'll be laughin'
singin'

128
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:50,130
And records playin'

129
00:08:50,190 --> 00:08:52,160
Dancin'in the street

130
00:08:52,230 --> 00:08:54,160
Look at those hooligans.

131
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:57,170
Actually, I think it's a wonderful
expression of freedom and joy.

132
00:08:57,230 --> 00:09:00,100
I'll tell you a wonderful expression
of freedom and joy.

133
00:09:00,170 --> 00:09:03,610
Twelve weeks of nothing but me at the
West Side Golf Course, and no Detweiler.

134
00:09:03,670 --> 00:09:05,730
I second that emotion, sir.

135
00:09:07,910 --> 00:09:09,840
Man, Teej,
that prank was sweet.

136
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:14,510
Yeah, you should've seen
Finster's face-- I thought
she was gonna blow a gasket.

137
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:16,520
Those limesicles were tasty.

138
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:18,520
A tasty beginning
to a tasty summer.

139
00:09:18,590 --> 00:09:21,520
Twelve weeks of nothing but
riding bikes, hanging out at the lake...

140
00:09:21,590 --> 00:09:23,790
and T.P.-ing
the West Side Golf Course.

141
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:26,090
Summer vacation--
the ultimate recess.

142
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:29,100
Yeah, I can't wait
to get to baseball camp.

143
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:31,100
Baseball camp ?
What are you talking about ?

144
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:34,100
Actually, Teej,
I'm gonna be out of town too.

145
00:09:34,170 --> 00:09:36,600
Big-time Wrestling Federation
has this training camp,

146
00:09:36,670 --> 00:09:39,540
and I gotta learn some new moves
if I'm ever gonna turn pro.

147
00:09:39,610 --> 00:09:41,740
- But, Spinelli--
- It's military camp for me.

148
00:09:41,810 --> 00:09:44,250
My dad says I need to
learn to be a leader.

149
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:46,750
I shall be attending
the Mt. Van Buren Space Camp.

150
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:50,620
- Don't wanna let those
science geeks get ahead of me.
- You're all going to camp ?

151
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:52,210
- Not me.
- Thank goodness.

152
00:09:52,290 --> 00:09:55,220
The Young Voices Training Program
doesn't like the word "camp."

153
00:09:55,290 --> 00:09:58,820
They provide opportunities for aspiring
singers to train their voices...

154
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:00,950
in a rigorous
yet supportive setting.

155
00:10:01,030 --> 00:10:02,960
But summer's gonna be ruined.

156
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:06,470
What am I gonna do ? Play baseball
by myself? Watch reruns ? Read ?

157
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,900
Sorry, man, but we gotta
think about our futures.

158
00:10:08,970 --> 00:10:12,130
Yeah, we can't waste the whole summer
just fooling around like kids.

159
00:10:12,210 --> 00:10:15,540
- But we are kids !
- Actually, as of the completion
of fourth grade,

160
00:10:15,610 --> 00:10:17,550
we are technically considered
pre-young adults.

161
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:19,740
And next year
we won't even be "pre."

162
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:21,750
But--
[ Sighs ]

163
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:25,550
All right, let's make the most
of the time we've got left.
When do you all leave ?

164
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:28,560
- First thing in the morning.
- Oh, man.

165
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:31,730
[ Chattering ]

166
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,000
Well, there's my bus.

167
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,500
- Better get going.
- Yeah, same here.

168
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:40,330
Bye, Teej.
Try to have some fun, okay ?

169
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,340
Don't worry, buddy.
You'll have a great time without us.

170
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:46,340
I don't know, Vince.
All my plans were made for six.

171
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:52,080
Don't tell me you Ashleys
are going to baseball camp.

172
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:54,080
Eeew !
As if!

173
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:56,950
Cheerleading camp
is right across the lake. Duh !

174
00:10:58,020 --> 00:10:59,780
I hope it's a big lake.

175
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:01,790
[ Horn Honks ]

176
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:06,130
Ah, space camp.

177
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,460
Wonder if they'll
let us make craters.

178
00:11:10,330 --> 00:11:13,270
Hey, Hustler Kid,
I didn't know you wrestled.

179
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,270
I don't.
I'm pre-management.

180
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:19,270
Besides, my research tells me
that kids who wrestle trade
the most for contraband snacks.

181
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:22,040
Which reminds me--
Wanna buy a Winger-Dinger ?

182
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:25,980
All right, all the kindergarten
performers on the bus first.

183
00:11:26,050 --> 00:11:27,980
-[ All Shouting ]
- Me Viking!

184
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:31,780
Me Viking !
Me Viking ! Me Viking !

185
00:11:31,850 --> 00:11:33,790
Bon voyage...

186
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:41,730
[ Adult Baritone ]
T.j.

187
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,730
[ Applause ]

188
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,730
Big kid sing good.

189
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,330
- Yeah.
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

190
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,340
Well, Teej,
there's my transport.

191
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:54,070
Why don't you come with ?
Military camp's gonna be a blast !

192
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:57,080
Griswald, you maggot,
get your fanny over here now !

193
00:11:57,150 --> 00:12:00,510
Thanks, Gus, but I think I'll
stick it out at home this summer.

194
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:04,250
Okay, but you don't know
what you're missing.

195
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:07,920
- Hiya, Captain Brad !
- I don't like you, Griswald.
I am not your friend !

196
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:11,950
- Do I make myself clear ?
- Yes, sir ! Not looking
for friendship, sir !

197
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:14,290
Good luck, Gus.
You're gonna need it.

198
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:18,130
Man, this summer's
gonna whomp.

199
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:24,970
One is
the loneliest number

200
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,200
That you'll ever do

201
00:12:29,510 --> 00:12:32,810
Two can be
as bad as one

202
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:39,790
It's the loneliest number
since the number one

203
00:12:43,890 --> 00:12:45,490
[ Bird Squawking ]

204
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:48,960
No is
the saddest experience

205
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:52,020
You'll ever know

206
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:56,970
Yes, it's
the saddest experience

207
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,010
You'll ever know

208
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,480
'Cause one
is the loneliest number

209
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:07,350
That you'll ever do

210
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:12,150
One is
the loneliest number

211
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:14,690
Whoa-ohh
worse than two

212
00:13:22,430 --> 00:13:24,870
And so, the summer season
officially begins...

213
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:28,370
with kids all over the country
rushing off to camp.

214
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,370
In other news, the national
No Recess movement...

215
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:33,370
has hit a serious
stumbling block...

216
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,380
with the disappearance
of its leader,

217
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,380
former Secretary of Education
Phillium Benedict.

218
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:41,540
Benedict, fired by the president
two years ago for his extremist views,
has recently been--

219
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:44,640
No recess ?
What a bunch of hogwash.

220
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,650
[ Yawns ]
Morning, Mom. Morning, Dad.

221
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:50,490
Are you just getting up now ?
Geez, you're sleeping away
your whole vacation.

222
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,990
Why don't you go play
with your friends ?

223
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:55,390
What friends ? The ones
who abandoned me and went to camp ?

224
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,400
Now, T.j., I know there are
other boys around this summer.

225
00:13:58,470 --> 00:14:01,330
Mrs. Ween says Randall is available.
Do you want me to make a play date ?

226
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,340
- A play date ?
- Bye, Mom. Bye, Dad.

227
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:04,900
Bye, T-jerk.

228
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:07,240
Now, Becky, be nice
to your little brother.

229
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:09,240
He's feeling S-A-D right now.

230
00:14:09,310 --> 00:14:12,770
- I can spell, Mom.
- Well, unlike some kids,
I gotta get to work.

231
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:15,780
Mr. Walsh says if I can
master the Vatman 2000,

232
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:19,250
I'll be assistant manager
by the end of the summer,
and you know what that means--

233
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:21,260
I'll get to drive
the Floppy Burger truck.

234
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,020
Boy, she's sure
aiming for the stars.

235
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:26,930
At least she's not sitting
around the house, moping all summer.

236
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,440
Going to a play date
with Randall.

237
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:36,940
Man, I can't believe
I sunk this low.

238
00:14:37,010 --> 00:14:38,940
This is the worst summer ever.

239
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:41,100
[ Loud Zap ]

240
00:14:44,110 --> 00:14:48,020
- What the heck ?
- [ Loud Zap ]

241
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,680
- That's weird.
- Hey,you!

242
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:51,550
Get away from that fence !

243
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:08,860
Hey, Dad, what do they
use the school for during the summer ?

244
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:11,130
They lock it up.
It's empty. Why ?

245
00:15:11,210 --> 00:15:14,270
Today, when I was riding by,
I saw this scary guy and--

246
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:16,140
I'm sure he was just
cleaning up.

247
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:20,110
I think something weird's going on
in there-- something really weird.

248
00:15:20,180 --> 00:15:22,620
[ Sighs ]
Mrs. La Salle was right.

249
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:24,980
We should've sent him
to some kind of camp.

250
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:38,530
9:3 2 a.m. Ugly bald guy
still guarding school.

251
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,740
[ Horn Honks ]

252
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,980
Staging area one.

253
00:15:52,050 --> 00:15:54,480
- Give me a hand with this.
- Got it.

254
00:15:54,550 --> 00:15:58,320
9:3 2-and-a-half a.m.
Grownups wrong. School's not empty.

255
00:15:58,390 --> 00:16:00,910
[ Loud Zap ]

256
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:06,990
9:3 2 and three quarters.
Green glow in window again.

257
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:09,090
I'm going in
for a closer look.

258
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:22,940
[ Loud Zap ]

259
00:16:23,010 --> 00:16:25,950
All right,
go ahead and elevate it.

260
00:16:32,090 --> 00:16:34,020
[ Gasps ]

261
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,190
Mom ! Mom !

262
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:40,020
- [ Groans ]
- T.j. ! Are you all right ?

263
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:43,190
Those guys at the school, they're doing
some kind of evil experiment !

264
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:46,130
That bonk on the head
must've rattled your little brain.

265
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:48,030
- But, Mom--
- You're feverish.

266
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:51,800
You wait right here.
I'll go get the baby thermometer
and the petroleum jelly.

267
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:53,710
Uh, Dad, Dad !

268
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,370
- Dad !
- What is it, boy ?

269
00:16:56,450 --> 00:16:58,880
Those bad guys have a laser beam
and they're lifting this safe--

270
00:16:58,950 --> 00:17:01,680
T.j., did you run into
the sliding glass door again ?

271
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:04,810
No, but-- Yeah, but--
Gaaah !

272
00:17:04,890 --> 00:17:08,220
Come back ! Your mom's gonna
want to take your temperature !

273
00:17:10,390 --> 00:17:14,060
Okay, kid,
we got it all in the report.

274
00:17:14,130 --> 00:17:17,060
We'll take care of
those mad scientists.

275
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:20,070
[ Chuckles ] Yeah, no one's gonna
levitate any safe on my watch.

276
00:17:23,370 --> 00:17:26,310
Ooh, look, Artie,
somebody's levitating my doughnut...

277
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:28,310
with a laser beam !

278
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:33,070
-[ Laughing Continues ]
- Go home, kid! Go home!

279
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:35,080
Laugh at me, will ya ?

280
00:17:35,150 --> 00:17:38,350
- I'm gonna be a taxpayer someday !
-[ Man ] Have a good round.

281
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,910
Principal Prickly !

282
00:17:41,990 --> 00:17:43,920
Wait !

283
00:17:48,930 --> 00:17:50,870
Yeah, you guys
did it right.

284
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:54,270
Psychology, law, waste management--
good, solid careers.

285
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:57,270
Me, I'm stuck with a bunch
of pain-in-the-neck kids all year.

286
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:01,330
- Pete, are you gonna putt
or grouse all day ?
- Okay, okay, here goes.

287
00:18:01,410 --> 00:18:03,340
-[ Tj.] Principal Prickly!
- Ohh !

288
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:07,780
You gotta come quick !
It's an emergency !

289
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:10,790
Well, well, well, if it isn't
Mr. Ice Cream For Everyone.

290
00:18:10,850 --> 00:18:13,790
- This is that kid
I was telling you about.
- The "saggy butt" kid ?

291
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:17,190
- Hey, hey, whatever happened to
doctor-patient confidentiality ?
- Sorry.

292
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:20,960
Something weird's
going on in the school.
I saw these mad scientists and--

293
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:24,900
Yeah, yeah, very funny.
I'm not falling for another one
of your so-called jokes.

294
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:27,400
- How dumb do you think I am ?
- It's not a joke, sir.

295
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:29,700
They have this laser beam, and--

296
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:32,900
Aw, please, Principal Prickly, you gotta
believe me ! The school's in danger !

297
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,910
Give me a break,
Detweiler.

298
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:36,910
Come on.
Go with the kid, Pete.

299
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:39,910
- This isn't the kind of issue
you should be avoiding.
- [ All Laughing ]

300
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:43,420
All right, Detweiler,
let's get this over with.

301
00:18:52,830 --> 00:18:56,090
Looks fine to me.
Now can I go back to my golf game ?

302
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:59,030
Just wait till you get inside.
You'll see.

303
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,660
Oh, the things I do
for you kids.

304
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:04,100
Sometimes I think you were
put on this Earth just to--

305
00:19:04,170 --> 00:19:07,270
- Aaah !
- Aaah !

306
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:14,620
Aaah !

307
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:27,320
[ Panting ]
1 1 :57 a.m.

308
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,330
Principal Prickly
dematerialized...

309
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,330
in a horrifying field
of electricity.

310
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:34,340
The cops won't listen.
Mom and Dad won't listen.

311
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:37,340
I gotta get the guys together.
It's the only way.

312
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,870
Like, I am so through
with him, Melissa.

313
00:19:40,940 --> 00:19:43,380
He asked me if I spoke French,
then winked at me.

314
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:46,380
Becky, you gotta help me !
I need a ride up to Chesterville !

315
00:19:46,450 --> 00:19:49,380
Are you kidding ? I'm not doing anything
for you, you little dork.

316
00:19:49,450 --> 00:19:52,890
"Oh, how I dream of the mustache fuzz
on jimmy's sweaty lips...

317
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,890
glistening as he cooks in the light
of a dozen hamburger heat lamps."

318
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:58,890
- Hey, that's my diary ! Give me that !
- Ah-ah-ah. I've got copies.

319
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:02,230
Either you give me a ride,
or this baby hits the Internet.

320
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:13,470
Get your motor runnin'

321
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:15,510
Head out on the highway

322
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,510
Thanks for driving me, Becky.

323
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,510
You're the sweetest big sister
a kid could ask for.

324
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:23,520
And you are the annoying pet monkey
I wish I never got!

325
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:25,520
Hey, I try to keep things
interesting.

326
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:28,280
Next rest stop, pull in.
I gotta take care of business.

327
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:33,290
Get that front leg up,
Biggles.

328
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,800
You call that a pitch,
Hornsby ?

329
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:38,800
Come on, La Salle !
Throw it, don't aim it !

330
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:40,800
I know, I know !

331
00:20:40,870 --> 00:20:43,800
Man, I can pitch just fine
when I'm with my friends.

332
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:45,900
Psst! Psst!

333
00:20:45,970 --> 00:20:49,740
- T.j., what are you doing here ?
- You gotta come back to town.
It's an emergency.

334
00:20:49,810 --> 00:20:51,610
What ? I can't just leave.

335
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:54,110
Something weird
is going on at school.

336
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:56,410
- Principal Prickly got dematerialized.
- Dematerialized ?

337
00:20:56,490 --> 00:20:59,480
- T.j., you're crazy.
- Am I ?

338
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:04,660
Mt. Van Buren ? That's 20 miles away.
I'm not taking you there.

339
00:21:04,730 --> 00:21:07,160
"Dear Diary,
I dreamed ofjimmy again.

340
00:21:07,230 --> 00:21:09,160
He was rocking me so gently,

341
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:13,400
-just like he rocks the grease off
a basket of hot and steamy onion rings."
- [ Moans ]

342
00:21:13,470 --> 00:21:15,900
- Whoa ! Let me look at that.
-jerks.

343
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:27,170
Hey, you kids ! Get away from
that fake Martian landscape !

344
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:30,180
- Miss Director ! Miss Director !
- What is it now, Gretchen ?

345
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:34,190
I've been studying the moon with the
200-inch telescope at the observatory,

346
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:37,190
and I've detected some peculiar
eccentricities in its orbit.

347
00:21:37,260 --> 00:21:41,960
Gretchen, maybe you should try out one
of these neat antigravity harnesses.

348
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:43,960
The other kids love 'em,

349
00:21:44,030 --> 00:21:46,970
and look, you can even do back flips,
just like real astronauts.

350
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,700
But--

351
00:21:48,770 --> 00:21:50,700
[ Sighs ]
Why do I bother ?

352
00:21:50,770 --> 00:21:53,170
Because you're driven
by a passionate desire for knowledge ?

353
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:55,470
T.j. ? Vince ?
What are you guys doing here ?

354
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:57,510
You're not gonna
believe this, but--

355
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,770
- Dematerialized ?
-just like out of Star Trek.

356
00:21:59,850 --> 00:22:01,780
Fascinating.

357
00:22:01,850 --> 00:22:04,110
Mi, mi, mi, mi, mi

358
00:22:04,190 --> 00:22:07,350
-   Mi, mi, mi, mi, mi
-   Mi, mi, mi, mi, mi

359
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:09,360
Mi, mi, mi, mi--
[ Whispering ]

360
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:11,120
Me ?

361
00:22:11,190 --> 00:22:14,860
Look out, marshals !
Here comes the flying press !

362
00:22:14,930 --> 00:22:16,860
[ Grunts ]

363
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:25,200
You are a pathetic excuse
for a soldier, Griswald!

364
00:22:25,270 --> 00:22:28,500
You will never be a leader !
Now, stand at attention until I return !

365
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:32,070
And do not move a muscle !
Do you hear me ? Not a muscle !

366
00:22:45,590 --> 00:22:49,030
- Thanks a lot, sis.
- You owe me gas money.

367
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:53,470
- Okay, Teej, what's this
big secret plot of yours ?
- Follow me.

368
00:22:55,970 --> 00:22:57,910
Look at that.

369
00:22:57,970 --> 00:23:00,000
Let's get movin' out.

370
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:03,070
- Who are those guys ?
- Perhaps they're government agents.

371
00:23:03,150 --> 00:23:05,080
- Or gangsters.
- Or aliens.

372
00:23:05,150 --> 00:23:07,240
Aliens ?
They don't look like aliens.

373
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,250
Well, maybe they're in disguise.

374
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:12,680
Yeah, if you were an alien,
you wouldn't just walk around
in your lizard skin all day.

375
00:23:12,750 --> 00:23:14,690
Hmm. Good point.

376
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:17,190
Whoever they are, we need
to take a closer look.

377
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:20,190
- We'll get the rest later.
- Right. I'll close it up.

378
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:22,200
Hurry.

379
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,270
Man, this thing weighs a ton.

380
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,970
That's 'cause it's full
of moon rocks and alien eggs.

381
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:45,050
Hey, it's just
a bunch of paper.

382
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:48,580
Weather maps ? Test scores ?
Some stuff written in Swedish ?

383
00:23:48,660 --> 00:23:52,750
- Actually, that's Norwegian.
- Whatever. It's all
just dumb school stuff.

384
00:23:52,830 --> 00:23:56,760
You got me out of baseball camp to watch
some guys restock the supply room ?

385
00:23:56,830 --> 00:23:59,430
No ! Something's going on
in the school ! I swear !

386
00:23:59,500 --> 00:24:03,440
Teej, I think you cooked
this whole thing up just 'cause
you wanted us back from camp.

387
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:05,440
- What ?
- Hey, we understand.

388
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:08,500
It must be pretty boring around here
all summer by yourself.

389
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:11,770
Your mind simply created an adventure
because it needed some excitement.

390
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:14,680
No, it really happened.
I saw Prickly disappear.

391
00:24:14,750 --> 00:24:16,650
Well, if Prickly disappeared,

392
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:18,620
then who's that ?

393
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:31,360
- Come on, guys. Let's get back to camp.
- Yeah.

394
00:24:31,430 --> 00:24:33,370
See ya in a few weeks, Teej.

395
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:36,200
No, wait !
You guys gotta believe me !

396
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:38,540
- I'm not making it up ! I-- I--
-[ Metal Clanking ]

397
00:24:38,610 --> 00:24:41,870
- Aye-yi-yi, yi-yi.
- [ All Gasp ]

398
00:25:00,300 --> 00:25:02,160
Whoa !
What's happening ?

399
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:09,740
[ Sputtering ]

400
00:25:16,780 --> 00:25:20,210
Okay, that right there ?
That was messed up.

401
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:24,380
[ Tj.]
Mikey?

402
00:25:24,450 --> 00:25:26,390
Mikey, you okay ?

403
00:25:26,450 --> 00:25:28,220
W-Where am I ?

404
00:25:28,290 --> 00:25:30,220
You're in T.j.'s backyard, man.

405
00:25:30,290 --> 00:25:32,350
How'd you guys
get me here ?

406
00:25:32,430 --> 00:25:34,360
Hey, this is kinda comfy.

407
00:25:34,430 --> 00:25:36,990
Yeah, yeah. Get out of there,
you big lummox.

408
00:25:37,070 --> 00:25:40,000
Okay, Teej, you were right. Something
weird is going on in the school.

409
00:25:40,070 --> 00:25:43,330
- And Prickly must be in on it.
- I say we go to the police.

410
00:25:43,410 --> 00:25:46,400
I already went to the police.
I went to everyone. Nobody'll listen.

411
00:25:46,470 --> 00:25:49,500
- What we need is proof.
- Proof? How are we gonna get proof?

412
00:25:49,580 --> 00:25:52,740
- I got a plan. A stakeout.
- A stakeout ?

413
00:25:52,810 --> 00:25:56,610
We can stay up in my tree house
and watch the school every night
until something happens.

414
00:25:56,690 --> 00:25:58,780
- Like one of them TV cop shows.
- Sure.

415
00:25:58,850 --> 00:26:02,020
The next time those laser guys make
a move, we'll catch 'em red-handed.

416
00:26:02,090 --> 00:26:04,720
We can take pictures
with my night-vision digital cam.

417
00:26:04,790 --> 00:26:07,730
Then we call in the feds
and, bang, we got 'em.

418
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:10,420
Only one problem--
What about camp ?

419
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:15,770
Oh, yeah. If my dad finds out
I've gone AWOL, he'll throw me
in the brig till September.

420
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:18,930
Not to worry. I'll get Becky to drive
you back to camp in the morning.

421
00:26:19,010 --> 00:26:22,880
Then at night we'll pick you up again.
Campers by day, spies by night.

422
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:25,610
But what if the camp counselors
notice we're not there ?

423
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:28,050
Leave that to me.

424
00:26:34,490 --> 00:26:36,860
- Call for you, sir.
- Give me that.

425
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:39,390
- Captain Brad here.
- Bradley. This is Colonel O'Malley.

426
00:26:39,460 --> 00:26:41,400
- Colonel O'Malley ?
- Your commanding officer !

427
00:26:41,460 --> 00:26:43,400
Oh ! Yes, sir !
Sorry, sir !

428
00:26:43,470 --> 00:26:47,200
I hear you've got a soldier there named
Griswald. Good man. One of the best.

429
00:26:47,270 --> 00:26:49,700
- H-He is ?
- You heard me ! He's officer material.

430
00:26:49,770 --> 00:26:52,210
I've had my eyes on him
for years.

431
00:26:52,270 --> 00:26:56,230
Now, pay attention, Bradley. I've got
Griswald on special assignment tonight.

432
00:26:56,310 --> 00:26:59,800
- When he gets back to camp,
act like nothing's happened.
- Yes, sir !

433
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:03,510
And you'd better start making his bed
and spit-shining his shoes as well.

434
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:05,950
That's all for now.
Carry on.

435
00:27:06,020 --> 00:27:08,150
Okay, Spinelli, you're next.

436
00:27:08,220 --> 00:27:10,850
Someone's wrestling
My Lord

437
00:27:10,930 --> 00:27:13,860
Kumbayah

438
00:27:13,930 --> 00:27:16,160
Heads are smashing
My Lord

439
00:27:16,230 --> 00:27:18,170
-[ Phone Rings ]
-   Kumbayah

440
00:27:18,230 --> 00:27:20,170
Speak to me.

441
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:22,170
-   Bones are cracking, My Lord
- Yeah ? Yeah ?

442
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:25,500
- I'll cover for you, Spinelli,
but it's gonna cost you.
-   Kumbayah

443
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:36,020
Oh, like, that is such the wrong
color for Vince. Put the blue one on.

444
00:27:37,420 --> 00:27:41,450
Ashley A, you totally
know how to accessorize.

445
00:27:43,530 --> 00:27:45,460
[ Boys Snoring ]

446
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,970
[ Whispering, Muttering ]

447
00:28:08,950 --> 00:28:11,380
Infrared night vision,
200-to-1 zoom.

448
00:28:11,450 --> 00:28:14,510
I gotta hand it to you, Gretch. You can
see the whole school with this thing.

449
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:18,420
You can make lots of handy devices out
of the spare parts in a family's garage.

450
00:28:18,490 --> 00:28:20,430
I once fashioned
a particle accelerator...

451
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:23,430
out of a broken hair dryer
and a four-slice toaster oven.

452
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:25,430
"Tonight, the magical moment
arrived.

453
00:28:25,500 --> 00:28:28,440
We met behind the drive-thru menu
and kissed passionately...

454
00:28:28,500 --> 00:28:32,440
as the sound of the deep fat fryer
faded into the night."

455
00:28:33,510 --> 00:28:36,440
Man, I wish I had
an older sister.

456
00:28:36,510 --> 00:28:39,450
Laugh if you will.
I think it's beautiful.

457
00:28:39,510 --> 00:28:42,950
Sorry I'm late, guys, but I had to
wait till my mom and dad fell asleep...

458
00:28:43,020 --> 00:28:45,950
before I could sneak out
with... the goodies.

459
00:28:46,020 --> 00:28:48,150
Roast beef and mashed potatoes !
My favorite !

460
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:50,160
Mmm. Mmm. Mmm.

461
00:28:50,230 --> 00:28:55,890
- I also managed to swipe this.
- Rocky Road ! My other favorite !

462
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:58,400
Hey, give me
some of that.

463
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:05,870
Excuse me, but aren't we supposed
to eat dinner before dessert ?

464
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:12,580
Good one, Gretch.

465
00:29:12,650 --> 00:29:14,980
You were right, Teej.
This is the life.

466
00:29:15,050 --> 00:29:18,640
Hanging out with friends,
eating ice cream, spying on bad guys.

467
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:21,120
It's the ultimate
kid experience.

468
00:29:21,190 --> 00:29:23,050
Too bad these days are numbered.

469
00:29:24,530 --> 00:29:26,790
Yeah, this is probably
the last summer...

470
00:29:26,860 --> 00:29:28,800
we'll get to do stuff like this.

471
00:29:28,860 --> 00:29:30,800
Kinda whomps, huh ?

472
00:29:32,230 --> 00:29:35,170
Hey, remember that summer
after second grade...

473
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:38,170
when we went down to the pond
every day to catch minnows ?

474
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:42,230
Or how about that summer we all
carved our initials in that tree
in the Wilsons' backyard ?

475
00:29:42,310 --> 00:29:44,240
And Spinelli
spelled hers wrong.

476
00:29:44,310 --> 00:29:46,750
Hey, I was seven.
And S's are tricky.

477
00:29:46,820 --> 00:29:48,750
[ Gus Sobbing ]

478
00:29:48,820 --> 00:29:51,910
What's your problem ? This is
the first summer you've lived here.

479
00:29:51,990 --> 00:29:55,920
I know, and I'll never
have any of those memories.

480
00:29:55,990 --> 00:29:58,750
[ Whimpering ]

481
00:29:58,830 --> 00:30:00,820
Know what I'll never forget ?

482
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:03,930
That song
T.j.'s sister taught us...

483
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,930
the first summer
after kindergarten.

484
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,430
Oh, yeah.
Back when she was nice.

485
00:30:08,500 --> 00:30:12,170
- How'd it go again ?
- [ Inhales Deeply ]

486
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:15,470
[ Adult Baritone ]
john jacob

487
00:30:15,540 --> 00:30:18,840
jingleheimer Schmidt

488
00:30:18,910 --> 00:30:24,910
His name is my name too

489
00:30:24,990 --> 00:30:27,680
[ All ]
Whenever I go out

490
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:29,780
The people always shout

491
00:30:29,860 --> 00:30:32,290
There goes john jacob
jingleheimer Schmidt

492
00:30:32,360 --> 00:30:34,020
[ Tempo Quickens ]
Na-Na-Na-Na, Na-Na-Na

493
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:37,360
john jacob
jingleheimer Schmidt

494
00:30:37,430 --> 00:30:40,630
His name
is my name too

495
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:43,870
Whenever I go out
the people always shout

496
00:30:43,940 --> 00:30:46,170
There goes john jacob
jingleheimer Schmidt

497
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:47,830
Na-Na-Na-Na
Na-Na-Na

498
00:30:47,910 --> 00:30:51,310
[ Whispering ]
john jacobjingleheimer Schmidt

499
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:54,140
His name
is my name too

500
00:30:54,220 --> 00:30:55,880
Whenever I go out

501
00:30:55,950 --> 00:30:57,350
The people always shout

502
00:30:57,420 --> 00:30:59,940
There goes JohnJacob
Jingleheimer Schmidt

503
00:31:00,020 --> 00:31:01,960
[ Fades ]
Na-Na-Na-Na, Na-Na-Na

504
00:31:02,020 --> 00:31:04,460
[ Loud Zapping ]

505
00:31:13,640 --> 00:31:16,570
Well, here we are, sir. But it's
just an old principal's office.

506
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:18,400
Why is it so important ?

507
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:26,540
Because, my academically
challenged young friend,

508
00:31:26,610 --> 00:31:29,210
it used to be mine.

509
00:31:36,460 --> 00:31:38,390
1 0:41 a.m.

510
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:41,900
Gang back at camp.
I'm goin' in alone.

511
00:31:49,870 --> 00:31:52,270
[ Man ]
Man, oh, man.

512
00:31:52,340 --> 00:31:55,280
I've heard of simple assignments,
but this one takes the cake.

513
00:31:55,340 --> 00:31:57,280
Yuck.

514
00:31:57,350 --> 00:31:59,210
Hey.

515
00:31:59,280 --> 00:32:01,710
1 0:43 a.m. I found
what appear to be...

516
00:32:01,780 --> 00:32:03,720
Principal Prickly's golf pants ?

517
00:32:03,790 --> 00:32:06,380
Fact is,you're gettin'
real good at this stuff.

518
00:32:06,450 --> 00:32:08,890
Yeah, you're a regular
Robert De Niro.

519
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:11,050
Hey, I'm a man
of many talents.

520
00:32:11,130 --> 00:32:14,150
- Principal Prickly ?
- But wasn't Mrs. Prickly suspicious ?

521
00:32:14,230 --> 00:32:17,930
You kiddin' ? It was like
taking candy from a baby.

522
00:32:20,200 --> 00:32:23,140
[ Laughing Continues ]

523
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:29,280
Double-knit polyester.
These are Prickly's all right.

524
00:32:29,340 --> 00:32:32,510
But why would the bald guy wanna pretend
to be Principal Prickly ?

525
00:32:32,580 --> 00:32:34,910
And where's the real
Principal Prickly anyway ?

526
00:32:34,980 --> 00:32:37,180
Wait a minute.
There's something in here.

527
00:32:37,250 --> 00:32:38,980
"Help me ?"

528
00:32:39,050 --> 00:32:41,490
It sounds like a desperate cry
for help.

529
00:32:41,560 --> 00:32:44,490
- Then Principal Prickly
must still be in the school.
- Being held captive !

530
00:32:44,560 --> 00:32:47,190
You know what that means,
don't you, guys ?

531
00:32:47,260 --> 00:32:49,530
We gotta go in there
and save him.

532
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:56,630
- Bikes ?
- Check.
- Walkie-talkie ?

533
00:32:56,700 --> 00:32:58,640
- Check.
- Rope with pointy thing ?
- Check.

534
00:32:58,710 --> 00:33:00,570
Good. Then let's go.

535
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:02,580
I still say this is nuts.

536
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:06,410
Breaking out of the school
I understand, but breaking in ?

537
00:33:08,780 --> 00:33:11,380
Oh, boy !
Ms. Finster's gonna love this.

538
00:33:11,450 --> 00:33:13,390
[ Whistling ]

539
00:33:17,230 --> 00:33:19,890
[ Groans ]

540
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:23,420
[ Grunting ]

541
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:25,430
-[ Doorbell Rings ]
- Dang.

542
00:33:25,500 --> 00:33:29,060
Ten more minutes, and the pizza
would've been free.

543
00:33:34,710 --> 00:33:37,300
[ Sighs ]
It's 9:00 at night, Randall.

544
00:33:37,380 --> 00:33:39,900
- What do you want ?
- It's about T.j. Detweiler.

545
00:33:39,980 --> 00:33:43,380
Randall, I'm off duty until Labor Day.
He's someone else's problem now.

546
00:33:43,450 --> 00:33:47,320
But he's got all his friends
together, and they're planning
to break into the school !

547
00:33:48,390 --> 00:33:50,320
A break-in, eh ?

548
00:33:50,390 --> 00:33:53,490
Not if Muriel P. Finster
has anything to say about it.

549
00:34:24,090 --> 00:34:26,530
- Told you, Ms. Finster.
- [ Chuckles ]

550
00:34:26,590 --> 00:34:30,220
I wonder if I can get 'em
tried as adults. Come on.

551
00:34:34,170 --> 00:34:36,100
Hold the rope, boy.

552
00:34:41,010 --> 00:34:42,940
-[ Rope Creaking ]
- Uh-oh.

553
00:34:43,010 --> 00:34:44,940
-[ Snap ]
- Aaaah !

554
00:34:45,010 --> 00:34:46,710
-[ Thud ]
-[ Groans ]

555
00:34:49,020 --> 00:34:53,110
[ Muffled ] Ms. Finster,
could you please get off of me ?

556
00:34:54,490 --> 00:34:57,190
[ Gretchen ]
My, this is somewhat creepy.

557
00:34:57,260 --> 00:35:00,790
Yeah. I've never been
in a empty school at night before.

558
00:35:00,860 --> 00:35:02,800
Heck, I'll bet no kid has.

559
00:35:02,860 --> 00:35:05,300
I wonder where the aliens went.

560
00:35:05,370 --> 00:35:08,930
They probably go back
to the mother ship at night.

561
00:35:11,840 --> 00:35:13,500
Quick. In here.

562
00:35:16,540 --> 00:35:18,980
[ Footsteps Passing ]

563
00:35:19,050 --> 00:35:21,280
Hey, this is
our old room.

564
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:30,460
I hope somebody's
feeding the gerbil.

565
00:35:30,530 --> 00:35:32,460
-[ Man Talking, Echoing ]
- Shh ! I hear something !

566
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:36,120
I want this system working now.
Do you hear me ? Now!

567
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:39,130
We're doing our best, sir. We've just
run into a few technical difficulties.

568
00:35:39,200 --> 00:35:41,130
It's coming from up there.

569
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:44,300
- Like what ?
- I think what Dr. Lazenby
is trying to say--

570
00:35:44,370 --> 00:35:47,310
Oh, I know what he's trying
to say. He's trying to--

571
00:35:47,380 --> 00:35:50,310
- What are you doing ?
- Finding out what's what.

572
00:35:50,380 --> 00:35:52,870
[ Men Continue Talking ]

573
00:36:04,330 --> 00:36:06,050
Bingo.

574
00:36:10,570 --> 00:36:12,500
[ Grunting ]

575
00:36:13,730 --> 00:36:16,170
I'm stuck.
[ Continues Grunting ]

576
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:18,400
Curse these
bodacious hips of mine.

577
00:36:18,470 --> 00:36:21,410
Randall, run back to my place
and get the butter.

578
00:36:23,740 --> 00:36:27,200
- Do you have any idea who
you're talking to, Laramie ?
- It's Lazenby--

579
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:31,720
That photon channeler
is a piece of equipment,
like a carburetor in your car!

580
00:36:31,790 --> 00:36:33,720
You're supposed to be
a brilliant thinker.

581
00:36:33,790 --> 00:36:36,420
Do you know what brilliant thinkers
are supposed to do ?

582
00:36:36,490 --> 00:36:38,750
They're supposed to think !

583
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:40,760
Whoa, what is
all this stuff?

584
00:36:40,830 --> 00:36:44,260
Well, against the far wall is what
looks to be a plutonium turbine.

585
00:36:44,330 --> 00:36:46,890
Closer ahead,you'll observe
a global electrode.

586
00:36:46,970 --> 00:36:49,900
To your right is
the laser device we saw earlier,

587
00:36:49,970 --> 00:36:53,100
and of course, that glowing orb--
an electron pulse generator.

588
00:36:53,170 --> 00:36:55,770
- The nerve center of the system.
- Shh ! The bad guys are talking.

589
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:58,780
- But, Dr. Benedict, please--
- No, let me make this
clear to you, Lazenby.

590
00:36:58,850 --> 00:37:01,710
We have a thing called
a window of opportunity.

591
00:37:01,780 --> 00:37:06,380
If we miss the window of opportunity,
then the project fails.

592
00:37:06,450 --> 00:37:08,390
And if the project fails,

593
00:37:08,460 --> 00:37:11,790
then I get very,
very... angry !

594
00:37:11,860 --> 00:37:13,790
Th-They may have
a point, sir.

595
00:37:13,860 --> 00:37:17,890
It seems the logistical problems
are a bit more complicated
than Dr. Steinheimer thought.

596
00:37:17,970 --> 00:37:21,800
Yes, it would be a lot easier
if we could move the laser
to a more appropriate location.

597
00:37:21,870 --> 00:37:25,400
This operation will be
executed as planned from right here !

598
00:37:25,470 --> 00:37:27,410
Have I made myself clear ?

599
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:29,410
- But, sir--
- No buts !

600
00:37:29,480 --> 00:37:33,880
It started at 3rd Street.
It is going to end at 3rd Street.

601
00:37:33,950 --> 00:37:36,210
Dr. Benedict,
we're ready for the test.

602
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,220
Coming.

603
00:37:41,860 --> 00:37:44,480
[ Scientist ]
Levels are good.

604
00:38:10,690 --> 00:38:12,810
- Ready ?
- I've been ready for decades.

605
00:38:12,890 --> 00:38:14,860
-just do it.
- Yes, sir.

606
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:16,860
Initiate photon channeling.

607
00:38:17,930 --> 00:38:19,690
Photon channeling initiated.

608
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:23,200
Set magnification
coordinates .073.

609
00:38:24,300 --> 00:38:25,700
Coordinates set.

610
00:38:25,770 --> 00:38:28,960
Engage tractor beam now.

611
00:38:31,070 --> 00:38:32,840
[ Continues Grunting ]

612
00:38:32,910 --> 00:38:35,840
[ Loud Zapping ]

613
00:38:35,910 --> 00:38:38,170
What are those kids
up to in there ?

614
00:38:40,250 --> 00:38:42,270
[ All Gasp ]

615
00:38:46,690 --> 00:38:49,780
A little more.
A little more.

616
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:53,790
- He's shooting at the moon.
- I told you they weren't aliens.

617
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:57,800
[ Beam Sputtering ]

618
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:05,470
-[ Turbine Winding Down ]
- Dr. Rosenthal,
why did the beam suddenly--

619
00:39:05,540 --> 00:39:09,530
Oh, what's the technical
word for it ? Stop ?

620
00:39:09,610 --> 00:39:12,310
W-Well, uh, as I believe
you were told before--

621
00:39:12,380 --> 00:39:14,310
"Told before" ?
[ Chuckles ]

622
00:39:14,380 --> 00:39:18,220
Do you think I care what I was told
before ? I'll do better next time.

623
00:39:18,290 --> 00:39:20,220
"Next time."
Isn't that cute.

624
00:39:20,290 --> 00:39:22,220
Rosenthal,
let me ask you something.

625
00:39:22,290 --> 00:39:24,220
Say you were a teacher--

626
00:39:24,290 --> 00:39:27,230
or even better, say,
the principal of a school--

627
00:39:27,290 --> 00:39:30,730
and you had to deal with a naughty child
who didn't know his place,

628
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:34,560
who kept telling you over and over
that he'd do better "next time."

629
00:39:34,640 --> 00:39:37,570
But he never did.
What would you do ?

630
00:39:37,640 --> 00:39:41,010
Oh, no. N-Not detention.
Not detention !

631
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:44,010
- Take him away !
- No, please ! I can fix it !

632
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:48,310
Don't do this to me-e-e !

633
00:39:50,820 --> 00:39:53,580
All right, who's
second-in-command ?

634
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:59,290
- Uh, I am, sir.
- Well, good. Now you're in charge.

635
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:03,800
And if I were you, I'd make sure
I had this machine working at
full power by tomorrow morning.

636
00:40:03,860 --> 00:40:06,260
- Do I make myself clear ?
- Y-Yes, sir.

637
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:10,970
Oh, dear,
I got spittle on my lapel.

638
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:13,060
Mmm.

639
00:40:13,140 --> 00:40:15,900
-[ Vince ] We gotta get out of here.
- Uh-oh.

640
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:17,970
- What is it ?
- I got that feeling.

641
00:40:18,050 --> 00:40:20,840
- Hold it in, big guy. Hold it in !
- I can't !

642
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:28,580
[ Loud Burp, Echoing ]

643
00:40:28,660 --> 00:40:30,590
What was that ?

644
00:40:30,660 --> 00:40:33,150
Someone had better
say "excuse me."

645
00:40:34,330 --> 00:40:36,230
[ All ]
Whoa !

646
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:38,730
Fenwick, who let children
into the school ?

647
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:40,730
U-Uh, n-not me, sir.

648
00:40:40,800 --> 00:40:43,570
- Well, get them !
- Run !

649
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:47,630
- [ Men Shouting ]
- There they are !

650
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,640
- [ All Gasp ]
- Huh ?

651
00:40:50,710 --> 00:40:53,740
Get off our planet,
alien scum !

652
00:40:53,810 --> 00:40:56,340
[ Groans ]

653
00:41:01,860 --> 00:41:03,790
Over there !

654
00:41:05,830 --> 00:41:08,490
- Get 'em ! Get 'em !
- Come back here !

655
00:41:14,270 --> 00:41:16,330
Huh ? Whoa !

656
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:18,060
[ Grunts ]

657
00:41:19,940 --> 00:41:22,640
- Hyah !
- Ninjas !

658
00:41:22,710 --> 00:41:25,800
- Hyah !
- Get 'em !

659
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:28,820
Ninjas ! Why'd they
have to be ninjas ?

660
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:31,150
[ All Shouting ]

661
00:41:34,050 --> 00:41:35,990
This way ! Hurry !

662
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:42,220
- Go ! Go ! Let's go ! Hurry up !
- Go ! Go ! Hurry up !

663
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:44,160
- Now you !
- But, Teej--
- Go !

664
00:41:47,470 --> 00:41:49,400
- Haaah !
- [ Gasps ]

665
00:41:49,470 --> 00:41:51,840
Save yourselves !

666
00:41:51,910 --> 00:41:54,900
- T.j. ! T.j. !
- It won't budge !

667
00:41:55,980 --> 00:41:57,910
[ Shouting Continues ]

668
00:42:00,250 --> 00:42:02,240
[ Grunts ]

669
00:42:06,990 --> 00:42:10,980
What thej.P. Morgan
is going on around here ?

670
00:42:13,460 --> 00:42:15,660
Let me go.
Let me go !

671
00:42:15,730 --> 00:42:18,660
I'm warning you !
I'm a black belt in origami !

672
00:42:18,730 --> 00:42:22,170
Well, well, well,
if it ain't the little snoop.

673
00:42:22,240 --> 00:42:25,000
- What ? I ain't no snoop.
- [ Tape Rewinding ]

674
00:42:25,070 --> 00:42:28,510
[ T.j. On Tape ] 9:3 2 a.m.
Ugly bald guy still guarding school.

675
00:42:29,640 --> 00:42:31,410
Heh-heh. Oops.

676
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:34,570
Let's go, snoop.
You're in big trouble now.

677
00:42:35,980 --> 00:42:38,920
Ow ! Ow ! Watch the jacket !
It's cotton !

678
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:46,590
[ Muffled Shouting ]

679
00:42:46,660 --> 00:42:49,190
Principal Prickly !
You're alive !

680
00:42:49,260 --> 00:42:52,200
- Oww ! Would you be careful !
- Boy, am I glad to see you.

681
00:42:52,270 --> 00:42:56,200
You won't believe what these
guys are doing. They've got
this big laser gun and--

682
00:42:56,270 --> 00:42:59,710
- Whoa, who took your pants ?
- Never mind, Detweiler.just untie me.

683
00:43:01,010 --> 00:43:03,270
- These knots are tight.
- Of course.

684
00:43:03,340 --> 00:43:06,470
I've been pulling at them
for the last day and a half.
They've chaffed my wrist.

685
00:43:06,550 --> 00:43:09,480
- Don't worry, sir.
My pals'll get us out of here.
- What makes you so sure ?

686
00:43:09,550 --> 00:43:12,380
You don't know my friends.
They'll get help. You'll see.

687
00:43:14,390 --> 00:43:17,820
So you're saying you just escaped
from a troop of ninja warriors ?

688
00:43:17,890 --> 00:43:21,450
- That's right !
- And they got a giant laser gun
in the school auditorium ?

689
00:43:21,530 --> 00:43:23,760
- Precisely !
- Which is aimed at the moon ?

690
00:43:23,830 --> 00:43:25,860
Thank heavens you understand !

691
00:43:32,770 --> 00:43:35,370
[ Grunts ]
I've almost got it.

692
00:43:35,440 --> 00:43:37,380
Careful, Detweiler.
That's my putting hand.

693
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:39,110
[ Door Lock Unlocking ]

694
00:43:42,150 --> 00:43:44,280
Hello, Pete.
Remember me ?

695
00:43:44,350 --> 00:43:47,290
Well, well, if it isn't
Phillium Benedict.

696
00:43:47,350 --> 00:43:50,950
- I should've known
you'd be the one behind this.
- You know this guy ?

697
00:43:51,030 --> 00:43:52,960
Ah, Pete and I
are old pals.

698
00:43:53,030 --> 00:43:56,960
Although the last time
we saw each other, Pete
was the one ruining my life.

699
00:43:57,030 --> 00:44:00,000
By the way, Pete, you like this suit ?
It's Italian. Raw silk. Nice, huh ?

700
00:44:00,070 --> 00:44:03,400
You always were more concerned
about appearances than people, Phil.

701
00:44:03,470 --> 00:44:06,770
Oh, Pete, come on.
There's no need to be rude.

702
00:44:06,840 --> 00:44:10,070
Not after I instructed my men
to take such special care of you.

703
00:44:10,140 --> 00:44:14,080
Special care ?
That's what you call gagging me,
tying me up and taking away my pants ?

704
00:44:14,150 --> 00:44:18,080
Had to. Otherwise, you might run off and
betray me, like you did the last time.

705
00:44:18,150 --> 00:44:20,090
But, hey,
look at the bright side.

706
00:44:20,150 --> 00:44:22,090
At least you've got company now.

707
00:44:22,160 --> 00:44:24,750
Let the boy go.
He can't do anything to you.

708
00:44:24,830 --> 00:44:27,060
[ Sighs ]
Same old noble Pete.

709
00:44:27,130 --> 00:44:30,650
- Always standing up
for the rights of children.
- You ?

710
00:44:30,730 --> 00:44:33,670
But, unfortunately,
I can't let anybody go right now.

711
00:44:33,730 --> 00:44:38,670
You see, this experimental, um,
night school that I'm running
is kind of a secret.

712
00:44:38,740 --> 00:44:42,270
I'm trying to show that my...
[ Chuckles ] adult students
can be trained...

713
00:44:42,340 --> 00:44:44,610
to be capable and productive
members of society.

714
00:44:44,680 --> 00:44:47,110
Well, if you're just
running a night school,

715
00:44:47,180 --> 00:44:49,880
then what's that giant laser gun
doing in the auditorium ?

716
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:58,960
What a rude and badly dressed
little boy you are.

717
00:45:02,060 --> 00:45:06,500
You should teach your pupils a little
respect for their superiors, Pete.

718
00:45:06,570 --> 00:45:11,000
But that would mean that you'd
have to know how to teach them
anything at all, wouldn't it ?

719
00:45:16,710 --> 00:45:18,640
Geez, how do you
know that jerk ?

720
00:45:18,710 --> 00:45:20,870
We went through
teacher training together.

721
00:45:20,950 --> 00:45:22,880
- You mean--
- That's right, Detweiler.

722
00:45:22,950 --> 00:45:25,040
That man is a rogue teacher.

723
00:45:28,060 --> 00:45:30,990
[ Prickly ]
It was back in the spring of'68.

724
00:45:31,060 --> 00:45:35,650
A different age.
We were all young, idealistic
and ready to change the world.

725
00:45:38,070 --> 00:45:40,000
[ Chattering ]

726
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:42,500
[ Rock ]

727
00:45:42,570 --> 00:45:45,660
Oh ! Ha ha ha.
Peace, Peter.

728
00:45:45,740 --> 00:45:48,900
Hey, Muriel, had a groovy time
at the Dead concert last night.

729
00:45:48,980 --> 00:45:52,340
You gonna be at the teach-in Saturday ?
We're gonna paint my Volkswagen.

730
00:45:52,410 --> 00:45:54,850
- Wouldn't miss it for the world.
- Groovy.

731
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:57,850
Yes, we all thought
we were pretty cool.

732
00:45:57,920 --> 00:46:00,680
- But one guy was the coolest of us all.
-[ Vehicle Approaching ]

733
00:46:00,750 --> 00:46:03,620
Phillium Benedict
was my best friend.

734
00:46:03,690 --> 00:46:06,630
He was smart,
he was handsome.

735
00:46:06,690 --> 00:46:10,600
He had just been named principal
of 3rd Street School.

736
00:46:10,660 --> 00:46:12,600
[ All Giggling ]

737
00:46:12,670 --> 00:46:16,860
So, Phillium, how's it feel
being the youngest principal
in the history of the state ?

738
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:18,870
Copacetic, baby.

739
00:46:18,940 --> 00:46:22,640
I mean, you know what they say:
Young is in, man, and old is out.

740
00:46:22,710 --> 00:46:24,640
Way out.

741
00:46:24,710 --> 00:46:28,040
Do you like the American flag
helmet, Pete ? It does go
with the leather jacket, right ?

742
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:30,280
You are one groovy educator, Phil.

743
00:46:30,350 --> 00:46:32,280
Cool. Follow me, my man.

744
00:46:32,350 --> 00:46:35,290
I wanna show you
my new principal's pad.

745
00:46:39,990 --> 00:46:41,720
Whoa !

746
00:46:45,530 --> 00:46:47,800
Psychedelic principalia.

747
00:46:47,870 --> 00:46:50,460
Pull up a bag, bro.
I wanna rap.

748
00:46:51,810 --> 00:46:55,300
- Lay it on me, man.
- You see, Pete, I been thinkin'.

749
00:46:55,380 --> 00:46:57,310
We're a new generation
of teachers, right ?

750
00:46:57,380 --> 00:46:59,740
It's time we shook things up
a little.

751
00:46:59,810 --> 00:47:02,250
I hear you, brother.
In fact, dig this.

752
00:47:02,320 --> 00:47:05,250
I was meditating to that new
Ravi Shankar album last night...

753
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:07,250
when I got
this righteous notion--

754
00:47:07,320 --> 00:47:10,260
What if we hold all our classes outside,
on the playground ?

755
00:47:10,320 --> 00:47:14,590
Imagine-- school, recess.
No boundaries.

756
00:47:14,660 --> 00:47:18,460
Hey, baby, that's a hip idea,
but I got a better thought here.

757
00:47:18,530 --> 00:47:21,060
As my first official act
as principal,

758
00:47:21,130 --> 00:47:24,500
I've decided...
to get rid of recess.

759
00:47:25,770 --> 00:47:27,710
What ? No recess ?

760
00:47:27,770 --> 00:47:30,710
But, Phil, for a kid,
recess is like a major play-in.

761
00:47:30,780 --> 00:47:33,210
It's the one time of day
they have any freedom.

762
00:47:33,280 --> 00:47:35,210
[ Sighs ]
Look, Pete,

763
00:47:35,280 --> 00:47:37,220
the '60s are over.

764
00:47:37,280 --> 00:47:41,880
All that peace and love
and freedom stuff, it was great
for pickin' up chicks,

765
00:47:41,960 --> 00:47:44,390
but it's not gonna
help my career.

766
00:47:44,460 --> 00:47:47,390
To do that, I gotta
make test scores go up,

767
00:47:47,460 --> 00:47:51,900
and to make test scores go up, I gotta
keep kids in class where they belong.

768
00:47:51,970 --> 00:47:55,490
That's why, starting tomorrow,
I am tuning out recess...

769
00:47:55,570 --> 00:47:57,970
once and for all.

770
00:47:58,040 --> 00:47:59,900
[ Prickly ]
Needless to say,

771
00:47:59,970 --> 00:48:02,410
Phillium's plan
didn't go over all that well.

772
00:48:02,480 --> 00:48:04,410
[ Shouting ]

773
00:48:04,480 --> 00:48:06,410
- [ Protester] What do we want ?
- [ Crowd ] Recess !

774
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:08,540
- When do we want it ?
- Now !

775
00:48:08,620 --> 00:48:11,210
- What do we want ? When do we want it ?
- Recess ! Now !

776
00:48:11,290 --> 00:48:15,150
Be cool, people, be cool.
You're bumming my mellowness.

777
00:48:15,220 --> 00:48:18,210
We'll be cool when you give our kids
their recess back.

778
00:48:18,290 --> 00:48:20,230
Hey, baby,
I'll do what I want.

779
00:48:20,290 --> 00:48:23,730
I'm principal of the school, and there's
nothing anyone can do about it. Dig ?

780
00:48:23,800 --> 00:48:26,730
[ Shouting Continues ]

781
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:29,500
[ Man ]
It's not right!

782
00:48:29,570 --> 00:48:33,870
- People, people, please calm down.
- [ Shouting Stops ]

783
00:48:33,940 --> 00:48:37,540
Mr. Prickly here has informed me
of this "no recess" proposal.

784
00:48:37,610 --> 00:48:40,550
Let me assure you that
as long as I'm superintendent,

785
00:48:40,610 --> 00:48:43,810
this radical plan will never
be carried out in this district.

786
00:48:43,880 --> 00:48:46,820
- [ Cheering ]
- Hey, man, you just don't get it !

787
00:48:46,890 --> 00:48:48,820
Of course I do, Benedict.

788
00:48:48,890 --> 00:48:50,820
- That's why I'm replacing you.
- What ?

789
00:48:50,890 --> 00:48:54,090
- Prickly, from now on,
you will be principal.
- Who, me ?

790
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,600
Oh, I see what's going down here.

791
00:48:56,660 --> 00:49:00,760
You tricked me, went around my back
to the man to get my job !

792
00:49:00,830 --> 00:49:04,100
- No, Phil, it's not like that at all.
- Yeah, right !

793
00:49:04,170 --> 00:49:07,110
Come on, Muriel baby,
let's blow this scene.

794
00:49:07,170 --> 00:49:11,700
No, Phil, it's over. I could never
be with a man who doesn't love recess.

795
00:49:11,780 --> 00:49:14,210
So you're against me too.

796
00:49:14,280 --> 00:49:18,340
Well, fine. I don't need you.
I don't need anyone !

797
00:49:18,420 --> 00:49:21,510
- Aaah !
- Phil ! You okay, man ?

798
00:49:21,590 --> 00:49:23,680
Don't touch me !

799
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,690
You took my chick.

800
00:49:26,760 --> 00:49:28,690
You took my job.

801
00:49:28,760 --> 00:49:31,200
Well, enjoy it while you can,
Petey boy,

802
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:33,200
'cause you're gonna pay.

803
00:49:33,270 --> 00:49:36,460
Somehow, someway,

804
00:49:36,540 --> 00:49:38,870
you're gonna pay.

805
00:49:38,940 --> 00:49:41,600
I never saw Phillium again.

806
00:49:41,680 --> 00:49:44,110
He quit teaching,
went into politics,

807
00:49:44,180 --> 00:49:46,110
eventually became
secretary of education--

808
00:49:46,180 --> 00:49:49,110
until the president fired him for
trying to get rid of recess again.

809
00:49:49,180 --> 00:49:51,120
Only this time
it was nationwide.

810
00:49:51,180 --> 00:49:54,950
So that guy's some weirdo ex-teacher
who wants to get rid of recess ?

811
00:49:55,020 --> 00:49:57,350
- Mm-hmm.
- Okay.

812
00:49:57,420 --> 00:49:59,450
Now it's personal.

813
00:50:00,730 --> 00:50:03,790
Let's see-- weather maps,
some stuff in Norwegian,

814
00:50:03,860 --> 00:50:05,800
a Farmer's Almanac.

815
00:50:05,870 --> 00:50:08,560
Must be something in here that'll
explain what that Dr. Benedict is doing.

816
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:11,570
I'll tell you one thing
he's not doing--

817
00:50:11,640 --> 00:50:15,070
having lunch tomorrow at 1 2:22
with his little girlfriend.

818
00:50:15,140 --> 00:50:17,800
Spinelli, that's the man's
personal date book.

819
00:50:17,880 --> 00:50:19,810
Well, it's mine now,

820
00:50:19,880 --> 00:50:23,650
and I guess Miss Luna Pergum is gonna
be at the restaurant all by herself.

821
00:50:23,720 --> 00:50:26,650
- Who did you say ?
- The girl whose name
is in here-- Luna Pergum.

822
00:50:26,720 --> 00:50:28,650
Must be some Italian chick.

823
00:50:28,720 --> 00:50:30,660
Lunae perigeum.
Of course !

824
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:33,160
- What are you talking about ?
- Don't you understand ?

825
00:50:33,230 --> 00:50:36,820
Lunae perigeum is no lady.
It's an event. Look.

826
00:50:36,900 --> 00:50:40,530
Once a month, the moon reaches the point
where it's closest to the Earth--

827
00:50:40,600 --> 00:50:45,300
lunar perigee, which in this case
happens to be 1 2:22 tomorrow afternoon.

828
00:50:45,370 --> 00:50:49,970
Maybe that's when that doctor
guy is gonna shoot his laser
at the moon and blow it up.

829
00:50:50,040 --> 00:50:51,980
Close guess,
but I have another theory.

830
00:50:52,050 --> 00:50:56,510
When I was up at space camp,
I observed some abnormalities
in the moon's position.

831
00:50:56,580 --> 00:50:59,880
I couldn't figure out what was
causing it, but now it all makes sense.

832
00:50:59,950 --> 00:51:04,050
Dr. Benedict's device is not a
laser beam at all. It's a tractor beam !

833
00:51:04,120 --> 00:51:07,790
You mean he's gonna plow the moon's
surface ? Whatever will he plant ?

834
00:51:07,860 --> 00:51:10,490
Not a tractor, you goombah.
A tractor beam.

835
00:51:10,560 --> 00:51:12,500
Like from
a science fiction movie.

836
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:14,400
Precisely.

837
00:51:14,470 --> 00:51:16,400
Theoretically,
if a powerful tractor beam...

838
00:51:16,470 --> 00:51:19,410
were shot at the moon
exactly at lunar perigee,

839
00:51:19,470 --> 00:51:21,670
it could move the moon
into another orbit.

840
00:51:21,740 --> 00:51:24,680
Move the moon ? But why
would anybody want to do that ?

841
00:51:24,740 --> 00:51:27,580
Who knows, Vince ?
Who knows ?

842
00:51:34,650 --> 00:51:37,180
[ Banging On Metal ]

843
00:51:38,430 --> 00:51:40,360
Here we are, sir.

844
00:51:40,430 --> 00:51:44,730
I can't believe you have been
creeping around in these vents.
They're school property.

845
00:51:44,800 --> 00:51:46,730
Dang ! The line's dead.

846
00:51:46,800 --> 00:51:50,700
Hey, what did you do
with the walkie-talkie
you confiscated from me last week ?

847
00:51:50,770 --> 00:51:53,710
Top drawer, on the right.
Just look what Phil's done to my office.

848
00:51:53,770 --> 00:51:57,000
I had it all nice and clean
for the summer.

849
00:51:57,080 --> 00:51:59,940
Packs of gum, yo-yos,
my old baseball--

850
00:52:00,010 --> 00:52:01,950
Hey, I've been looking
for this.

851
00:52:02,020 --> 00:52:03,950
Here it is--
my walkie-talkie.

852
00:52:04,020 --> 00:52:06,450
Now all I gotta do is
contact the guys and--

853
00:52:06,520 --> 00:52:08,450
- Oh, no.
- What is it, Detweiler ?

854
00:52:11,120 --> 00:52:14,120
I told 'em
that guy was a nut.

855
00:52:14,190 --> 00:52:16,130
[ T.j. ] Hello !
Hello ! Is anybody there ?

856
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:18,630
It's T.j. !
T.j., buddy, you're okay ?

857
00:52:18,700 --> 00:52:21,630
- Yeah, I'm fine,
and so is Principal Prickly.
- Principal Prickly ?

858
00:52:21,700 --> 00:52:25,140
I don't have time to explain,
but I think we've figured out
what Benedict is up to.

859
00:52:25,210 --> 00:52:28,140
He's trying to get rid
of summer vacation !

860
00:52:29,480 --> 00:52:31,410
No !

861
00:52:31,480 --> 00:52:34,910
Guys, don't freak out on me !
I got a plan ! All we do is--

862
00:52:36,320 --> 00:52:41,080
Heh-heh. Why, Mr. Bald Guy,
what a surprise.

863
00:52:41,150 --> 00:52:42,820
T.j. ! T.j. !

864
00:52:42,890 --> 00:52:44,650
- It's dead !
- They must've got him !

865
00:52:44,720 --> 00:52:46,660
What are we gonna do ?

866
00:52:46,730 --> 00:52:49,490
There's only
one thing we can do:

867
00:52:49,560 --> 00:52:51,500
we gotta get help.

868
00:52:51,570 --> 00:52:54,730
[ Becky ] Bow-wow ! Welcome to Floppy
Burger. May I take your order, please ?

869
00:52:54,800 --> 00:52:57,270
- Becky, this is Vince.
- [ Becky ] What are you doing here ?

870
00:52:57,340 --> 00:53:00,930
It's not just Vince, it's me,
Gretchen, everybody. We got a problem !

871
00:53:01,010 --> 00:53:05,570
I got a problem too-- six dweeby
ten-year-olds who won't leave me
alone, even when I'm at work.

872
00:53:05,650 --> 00:53:08,580
I am a professional ! So whatever
your little problem is, forget it !

873
00:53:08,650 --> 00:53:11,450
- But it's about T.j.
- He's in trouble,
and he needs your help.

874
00:53:11,520 --> 00:53:13,450
[ Becky ]
Well, isn't that nice ?

875
00:53:13,520 --> 00:53:16,460
After stealing my diary, threatening
to put it on the Internet...

876
00:53:16,520 --> 00:53:19,460
and making me drive across the
state three times, he needs my help ?

877
00:53:19,530 --> 00:53:22,650
Give me one good reason
why I should help him.

878
00:53:22,730 --> 00:53:26,390
'Cause he's your little brother,
and he needs you.

879
00:53:26,470 --> 00:53:29,460
Please pull forward to
the second drive-thru window.

880
00:53:31,810 --> 00:53:34,240
A confiscated
walkie-talkie.

881
00:53:34,310 --> 00:53:39,640
Why do you do these things ? Do you
enjoy tormenting me ? Do you hate me ?

882
00:53:39,710 --> 00:53:42,710
I don't hate you, Phil.
I just think you're insane.

883
00:53:42,780 --> 00:53:44,720
[ Chuckles ]
Insane.

884
00:53:44,780 --> 00:53:46,720
Well, there you go again, Pete.

885
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:50,550
Insulting me, hurting my feelings,
just like 30 years ago.

886
00:53:50,620 --> 00:53:54,320
Only this time, Petey,
I'm ready.

887
00:53:54,390 --> 00:54:00,090
You see, all those years, no matter
how big I got, no matter how successful,

888
00:54:00,170 --> 00:54:02,330
I always thought about you.

889
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:05,740
How you embarrassed me !
How you humiliated me !

890
00:54:05,810 --> 00:54:08,740
How you destroyed my relationship
with Muriel Finster,

891
00:54:08,810 --> 00:54:10,740
the only woman I ever loved !

892
00:54:10,810 --> 00:54:13,340
- That part still grosses me out, sir.
- Shh.

893
00:54:13,410 --> 00:54:16,350
This time, Pete,
I'm gonna humiliate you.

894
00:54:16,420 --> 00:54:20,220
I'm gonna prove to the world
that you were wrong and I was right.

895
00:54:20,290 --> 00:54:22,220
- About what ?
- About recess !

896
00:54:22,290 --> 00:54:24,220
About freedom !
About test scores !

897
00:54:24,290 --> 00:54:26,690
I've found a way
to prove my theory.

898
00:54:26,760 --> 00:54:29,700
I'm gonna get rid of
the biggest recess of them all.

899
00:54:29,760 --> 00:54:32,700
I am gonna get rid
of summer vacation.

900
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:36,570
- You fiend !
- "Fiend." Try to help people,
that's the thanks you get.

901
00:54:36,640 --> 00:54:41,010
- It'll never work, Phil.
- Well, actually, Pete,
that's where you're wrong.

902
00:54:45,580 --> 00:54:50,310
You see, all I have to do is modify
the moon's orbit ever so slightly,

903
00:54:51,750 --> 00:54:54,910
and tide levels on the Eastern Seaboard
rise eight feet.

904
00:54:54,990 --> 00:54:56,920
Move the moon over here,

905
00:54:56,990 --> 00:55:00,590
and the currents that warm California
suddenly become ice-cold.

906
00:55:00,660 --> 00:55:03,600
Summer, as we know it,
will become a thing of the past.

907
00:55:03,660 --> 00:55:05,430
And without summer,

908
00:55:07,100 --> 00:55:10,040
- [ Both Gasp ]
- no summer vacation.

909
00:55:10,100 --> 00:55:13,040
- You'll never get away
with this, Benedict.
- Oh, yeah ?

910
00:55:13,110 --> 00:55:16,040
Well, who's gonna stop me ?

911
00:55:17,780 --> 00:55:20,210
Wow, I can't believe
my little brother...

912
00:55:20,280 --> 00:55:22,710
actually stumbled on
a real, live evil conspiracy.

913
00:55:22,780 --> 00:55:26,720
- That's our Theodore.
- You should see the crates
of soda they left back there.

914
00:55:26,790 --> 00:55:29,720
And boxes of mustard
and ketchup too.

915
00:55:29,790 --> 00:55:31,720
Mmm, tomato-ey.

916
00:55:31,790 --> 00:55:34,730
Hey, that's stuff's the property of
Floppy Burger International.

917
00:55:34,790 --> 00:55:37,960
Quit your gabbin' and step on it.
We need reinforcements.

918
00:55:41,500 --> 00:55:43,940
[ Cheering, Shouting ]

919
00:55:46,570 --> 00:55:48,510
[ Cheering, Shouting ]

920
00:55:57,580 --> 00:56:00,450
[ Finster ] I'm telling you,
a troop of ninja warriors...

921
00:56:00,520 --> 00:56:04,120
is using 3rd Street School as
a secret jujitsu training ground.

922
00:56:04,190 --> 00:56:08,130
- Ninja warriors. Elementary school.
- [ Snickering ]

923
00:56:08,190 --> 00:56:10,130
Jujitsu training ground ?

924
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:14,030
Hey, lady, aren't you forgetting
the magic laser beam ?

925
00:56:14,100 --> 00:56:16,470
- I'm serious !
- So are we.

926
00:56:16,540 --> 00:56:19,970
Hey, I got an idea-- Why don't you
go home, get some rest...

927
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:22,470
and we'll make a personal call
tojackie Chan.

928
00:56:22,540 --> 00:56:25,980
Yeah, he's the perfect man
for a job like this.

929
00:56:26,050 --> 00:56:29,450
I'm telling ya, something is
going on in that school !

930
00:56:29,520 --> 00:56:32,110
Help ! Help !
Somebody get us outta here !

931
00:56:32,190 --> 00:56:34,680
- Calm down, Detweiler.
- Calm down ?

932
00:56:34,750 --> 00:56:37,850
We're locked in a giant birdcage
while a madman's trying to
destroy summer vacation,

933
00:56:37,920 --> 00:56:39,860
and you want me
to calm down ?

934
00:56:39,930 --> 00:56:43,020
- I understand, but I--
- How can you understand ?
You're just a grownup.

935
00:56:43,100 --> 00:56:46,120
What do you know
about summer vacation ?

936
00:56:46,200 --> 00:56:49,130
I'll let you in on
a little secret, Detweiler.

937
00:56:49,200 --> 00:56:52,140
Every adult you've ever known
was a kid some time in his life.

938
00:56:52,210 --> 00:56:54,640
You think we don't
remember summer vacation ?

939
00:56:54,710 --> 00:56:59,080
Riding bikes by the creek ?
Catching polliwogs in a jar ?
Camping out under the stars ?

940
00:56:59,150 --> 00:57:01,380
Well, you're wrong.

941
00:57:01,450 --> 00:57:05,380
Some days I sit in my office, looking
out at you kids on the playground,

942
00:57:05,450 --> 00:57:08,390
and I think, "They don't know
how good they've got it.

943
00:57:08,460 --> 00:57:11,390
In a few years, they're all
going to be grownups, like me,

944
00:57:11,460 --> 00:57:14,390
and all those good times will
just be memories for them too."

945
00:57:14,460 --> 00:57:18,400
So go ahead, put a whoopee cushion in my
chair, cover my carpet with fake vomit,

946
00:57:18,470 --> 00:57:20,400
make fun of
my big, saggy butt.

947
00:57:20,470 --> 00:57:23,900
But don't you ever say I don't care
about summer vacation,

948
00:57:23,970 --> 00:57:27,740
'cause those memories are the last
part of childhood I've got left.

949
00:57:28,810 --> 00:57:31,570
Principal Prickly,
I had no idea.

950
00:57:31,640 --> 00:57:33,580
Yeah, well, now you do.

951
00:57:33,650 --> 00:57:37,080
- So let's stop messing around.
- How did you get those keys ?

952
00:57:37,150 --> 00:57:40,090
Swiped 'em off Phillium's desk
when he wasn't looking.

953
00:57:40,150 --> 00:57:43,090
Now come on.
We've got a summer vacation to save.

954
00:57:44,660 --> 00:57:47,850
[ All Chattering ]

955
00:57:47,930 --> 00:57:51,860
People ! People !
Just quiet down for a moment !

956
00:57:51,930 --> 00:57:53,870
Oh, man, nobody's listening.

957
00:57:53,930 --> 00:57:57,370
They'll listen to me, once I introduce
them to my good friend Madam Fist.

958
00:57:57,440 --> 00:58:00,300
Come on, Spinelli.
That's your answer for everything.

959
00:58:00,370 --> 00:58:03,810
I don't see you coming up
with any great ideas, sports boy.

960
00:58:03,880 --> 00:58:06,810
Listen to the two of you.
You're not helping at all.

961
00:58:06,880 --> 00:58:09,310
[ All Arguing ]

962
00:58:09,380 --> 00:58:13,380
[ Gus ]
Quiet!

963
00:58:13,450 --> 00:58:15,390
What we need is a leader.

964
00:58:15,460 --> 00:58:17,390
A kid with
the right training.

965
00:58:17,460 --> 00:58:20,050
A kid who knows strategy
and field tactics.

966
00:58:20,130 --> 00:58:22,060
A kid who commands respect.

967
00:58:22,130 --> 00:58:25,220
Yeah, but where we gonna
find a kid like that ?

968
00:58:25,300 --> 00:58:28,290
Leave that to me.

969
00:58:28,370 --> 00:58:30,960
- [ Chattering Continues ]
-[ Gretchen Whistles ]

970
00:58:31,040 --> 00:58:33,900
Please !
We have to get organized.

971
00:58:33,970 --> 00:58:35,910
Ah, what's the use ?

972
00:58:35,980 --> 00:58:37,910
If what you say is true,

973
00:58:37,980 --> 00:58:40,910
all the fun of being a kid
is, like, totally ruined anyway.

974
00:58:40,980 --> 00:58:44,140
- It's like the whole world's
been turned right side up.
- [ All Agreeing ]

975
00:58:44,220 --> 00:58:48,090
Not necessarily. All we have to do is
work together and come up with a plan.

976
00:58:48,150 --> 00:58:52,420
- Detweiler's the one who always
comes up with the plans.
- Let's face it-- we're doomed.

977
00:58:52,490 --> 00:58:55,930
- [ All Agreeing ]
-[ Spinelli ] That's what you think!

978
00:58:56,000 --> 00:58:59,800
Kids of the playground, meet
your new commanding officer.

979
00:59:04,000 --> 00:59:07,770
Griswald ? He couldn't
lead a glee club.

980
00:59:12,810 --> 00:59:14,870
You find that funny,
Bradley ?

981
00:59:14,950 --> 00:59:17,940
Well, I'm not here to make jokes !
I'm here to make history !

982
00:59:18,020 --> 00:59:20,450
So if you wanna laugh,
take it somewhere else.

983
00:59:20,520 --> 00:59:25,180
But if you wanna save the world, then
suck in your gut and stand at attention.

984
00:59:25,260 --> 00:59:27,520
Now who's with me ?

985
00:59:27,590 --> 00:59:30,530
[ Kazoos Playing
"River Kwai March"]

986
00:59:53,150 --> 00:59:56,140
[ Screams ]
Soda bomb ! Soda bomb !

987
00:59:56,220 --> 00:59:59,890
[ Gus ] Vince,you and the Ashleys
will be in charge of unit "A. "

988
00:59:59,960 --> 01:00:03,260
I'll take unit "B."
Spinelli, you get the special forces.

989
01:00:03,330 --> 01:00:05,560
- Special forces ?
- The kindergartners.

990
01:00:05,630 --> 01:00:09,570
- I owe you for this, Griswald.
- Now there's one last thing
I need to say.

991
01:00:09,640 --> 01:00:14,130
- [ Talking Ceases ]
- This mission is bigger than
any one of us kids.

992
01:00:14,210 --> 01:00:17,700
Bigger than T.j.
Even bigger than Principal Prickly.

993
01:00:17,780 --> 01:00:20,680
This, my friends,
is about the future.

994
01:00:20,750 --> 01:00:23,740
- Geez, he sounds like T.j.
- Shh. He's on a roll.

995
01:00:23,820 --> 01:00:27,980
Years from now when kids who aren't
even born yet look back on this moment,

996
01:00:28,050 --> 01:00:29,990
they'll say,
"They did it.

997
01:00:30,060 --> 01:00:32,460
Those kids saved
3rd Street School.

998
01:00:32,530 --> 01:00:34,860
They saved summer vacation."

999
01:00:36,160 --> 01:00:38,220
So, boys and girls,

1000
01:00:38,300 --> 01:00:40,930
we're goin' in.

1001
01:00:42,440 --> 01:00:45,100
- Twenty-two minutes to perigee, sir.
- Very good, Fenwick.

1002
01:00:50,980 --> 01:00:53,740
[ Men Chattering Indistinctly ]

1003
